@startuml state-target
!include style.iuml
title Target status

state "evaluate" as C <<choice>>
state "maintenance" as M : set by a maintainer or platform admin,\nwith reason. Nobody deploys,\nno auto-deploy.
state "deploying" as D : a pending or running deployment\n(never for preview targets,\nthey have one slot per PR)
state "locked" as L : lockable target, lock until in the future.\nHolder deploys, maintainers override.
state "available" as A : developers and maintainers deploy

[*] --> C
C --> M : [maintenance]
C --> D : [else if active deployment]
C --> L : [else if lockable and locked]
C --> A : [else]

A --> C : deploy requested
L --> C : deploy by holder or override,\nlock released or expired
D --> C : deployment finished
M --> C : maintenance off
A --> M : maintenance on
L --> M : maintenance on
D --> M : maintenance on

note bottom of C
  The server computes the status on every
  request. The first matching guard wins:
  maintenance > deploying > locked > available.
end note
@enduml
